"# Geometry

[fixture](../../index.md) › [fixture.java](index.md) · Every page: [llms.txt](../../llms.txt)

Class in [\`fixture.java\`](index.md). Since 1.0. Null-marked: types are non-null unless annotated.

\`\`\`java
public final class Geometry
\`\`\`

Inheritance: [\`Object\`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/Object.html) > \`Geometry\`

Operations on [\`shapes\`](Shape.md).

Every method is *pure*: it never modifies its arguments. **Thread safety:** every method is safe to call concurrently.

- [\`largest(Collection)\`](Geometry.md#largest%28java.util.Collection%29) picks the largest shape.
- [\`totalArea(Shape...)\`](Geometry.md#totalArea%28fixture.java.Shape...%29) sums areas.

1. First, measure.
2. Then compare, with \`compareTo\`.

Unit factors

| Unit | Factor |
| --- | --- |
| [\`Units.METERS\`](Units.md#METERS) | 1.0 |
| [\`Units.FEET\`](Units.md#FEET) | 0.3048 |

\`\`\`java
Shape big = Geometry.largest(List.of(Circle.of(1), Rect.square(2)));
double total = Geometry.totalArea(big, Circle.of(3));
\`\`\`

> Measure twice, cut once.

## Edge cases

Text with an entity — a superscript kept as raw markup, a line  
 break, a [hyperlink](https://example.com/spec), and \\<angle brackets\\> as literal text.

> **Implementation note**
>
> Areas are computed in double precision.

**See also**

- [\`Shape\`](Shape.md)
- [\`the area of a shape\`](Shape.md#area%28%29)
- "Euclid, Elements, Book I"
- [Area](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Area)

## Nested types

- [\`Geometry.Legacy\`](Geometry.Legacy.md) (class): Methods from before null markings; their nullness is unspecified.

## Fields

### PRECISION

\`\`\`java
public static final int PRECISION
\`\`\`

The default number of significant digits: \`6\`.

Constant value: \`6\`

### NAME

\`\`\`java
public static final String NAME
\`\`\`

The library's name, [\`"fixture"\`](Geometry.md#NAME), as tools report it.

Constant value: \`"fixture"\`

## Methods

### largest(Collection)

\`\`\`java
public static <T extends Shape & Comparable<? super T>> T largest(Collection<? extends T> shapes)
\`\`\`

Returns the largest shape.

**Type parameters**

- \`<T>\`: the shape type

**Parameters**

- \`shapes\` [\`Collection\`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/util/Collection.html)\`<? extends T>\` (non-null): the shapes; not empty

**Returns** \`T\`: the largest of \`shapes\`

**Throws**

- [\`NoSuchElementException\`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/util/NoSuchElementException.html) (unchecked): if \`shapes\` is empty

> **Implementation requirements**
>
> Compares with [\`Comparable.compareTo(Object)\`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/Comparable.html#compareTo%28T%29), keeping the first of equal shapes.

### totalArea(Shape...)

\`\`\`java
@Measured(precision = 6)
public static double totalArea(Shape... shapes)
\`\`\`

Sums the shapes' areas.

**Parameters**

- \`shapes\` [\`Shape\`](Shape.md)\`...\` (non-null): the shapes

**Returns** \`double\`: the total area in square meters; \`0\` for no shapes

### parse(String)

\`\`\`java
public static Shape parse(String text) throws IOException, ParseException
\`\`\`

Parses a shape from its text form, such as \`circle 2.5\`.

**Parameters**

- \`text\` [\`String\`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/String.html) (non-null): the text form

**Returns** [\`Shape\`](Shape.md) (non-null): the shape

**Throws**

- [\`IOException\`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/io/IOException.html): if the text names a file that cannot be read
- [\`IllegalStateException\`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/lang/IllegalStateException.html) (unchecked): if the parser was closed
- [\`ParseException\`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/text/ParseException.html): No description.

> **API note**
>
> The text form is not stable across releases; store shapes some other way.

### sum(List)

\`\`\`java
@Deprecated(since = "1.1", forRemoval = true)
public static double sum(List<Shape> shapes)
\`\`\`

> **Deprecated for removal since 1.1.**
>
> Use [\`totalArea(Shape...)\`](Geometry.md#totalArea%28fixture.java.Shape...%29), which takes any number of shapes.

Sums the areas of a list of shapes.

**Parameters**

- \`shapes\` [\`List\`](https://docs.oracle.com/en/java/javase/25/docs/api/java.base/java/util/List.html)\`<\`[\`Shape\`](Shape.md)\`>\` (non-null): the shapes

**Returns** \`double\`: the total area

### find(Map, String)

\`\`\`java
public static @Nullable Shape find(Map<String, ? extends Shape> shapes, String name)
\`\`\`

Since 1.1.

Finds a shape by name.

